  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Evaluate the repeated integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{3}^{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{3}^{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}[{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}[\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y]_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{e}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{e}^{-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}(3+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{[\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{{3}^{1}-{3}^{0}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
